1	// `andesim profile [--engine <id>] [report flags] ELF [-- <qemu args>]`.
2	//
3	// Hot inner-loop detection on the FUNCTIONAL engine, configured like the
4	// hybrid fast leg: profile picks a cycle-accurate engine (--engine or the
5	// sole one, the same selector cycle/hybrid use) and derives the QEMU launch
6	// from it -- the CPU model from the engine's `--print-qemu-config` driver
7	// globals, vlen from its --describe, and the staged qemu.cfg as -readconfig.
8	// That keeps the profiled ISA identical to the engine the reported
9	// `measure: --pc-start/--pc-end` windows will be measured on (a wrong vlen
10	// changes vsetvl trip counts, i.e. the hot-loop ranking itself).
11	//
12	// QEMU runs the ELF to completion with the hotIterationLoop TCG plugin; the
13	// plugin's
14	// `-d plugin -D` log is parsed, filtered (min-iters, RVV-only), nested, and
15	// rendered as the LLM Markdown report (or --no-llm table). All pure logic
16	// lives in profile.cpp; this file owns the IO: engine resolve, the cfg probe,
17	// the QEMU spawn, objdump/addr2line, and the per-loop symbol lookups.
